  "result": "I added `bulkArchiveIssuesSchema` (with `BulkArchiveIssuesInput`), `findIssuesByIds` and `bulkArchiveIssues` as specified. `tsc --noEmit` passes, but I didn't write or run any tests for the new code.\n\n`bulkArchiveIssues` follows the rules you listed and reuses the single-archive pieces: `assertOrgScope`, `assertCan(actor, \"issue:archive\", …)` and `issueRepo.archiveIssue`. It emits `issue.archived` once per archived issue. Duplicate ids are collapsed by the service, not the schema.\n\nTwo behaviours to be aware of:\n- **Permission check:** every remaining issue is checked before anything is written or published. One denial rejects the whole call with `PermissionDeniedError`.\n- **Not atomic after the check:** the archiving itself is per-issue, not in one transaction. If the database throws partway through, the earlier issues stay archived and already have their events.\n\nThe changes are in `src/schemas/issue.ts`, `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts` and `src/server/services/issue-service.ts`.",
